{
  "format": "worldspec-1",
  "name": "muddy-children",
  "title": "Muddy children (muddy-children)",
  "statements": [
    [
      1,
      "Three children are playing. Two of them, Amy and Ben, have mud on their foreheads; Cal does not."
    ],
    [
      2,
      "Each child can see the other children's foreheads but not his or her own."
    ],
    [
      3,
      "Their father says to all of them: \"At least one of you has mud on your forehead.\""
    ],
    [
      4,
      "Then he asks, again and again: \"Do you know whether you have mud on your forehead?\" All the children answer at the same time, truthfully, \"yes\" or \"no\"."
    ],
    [
      5,
      "Every child reasons perfectly and knows that the others do too, and every child hears every answer."
    ],
    [
      6,
      "The goal is to find in which round each child first answers \"yes\", and why."
    ]
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    {
      "id": "A-MC1",
      "kind": "intent",
      "text": "The eight possible patterns of mud are world objects; muddy and clean say each child's forehead in each world; view-mate(c, w, w2) holds when w2 differs from w only on c's own forehead (what c cannot see). The actual world is w-mmc.",
      "stmts": [
        1,
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "A-MC2",
      "kind": "intent",
      "text": "Knowledge is explicit (JL, 16 Nov 2026): knows-at(c, w, r) holds when, in world w at round r, no world c cannot tell from w is still possible. It and the other derived relations use negation only in their definitions; operators test them positively.",
      "stmts": [
        2,
        4,
        5
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "A-MC3",
      "kind": "intent",
      "text": "The father's statement and each round are operators that rule out worlds (out-at(w, round)), on every world at once. A world is live at round r if it was not ruled out in an earlier round, so each round is judged on the worlds left before it. A stage number keeps the order; round objects carry their number.",
      "stmts": [
        3,
        4,
        5
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "A-MC4",
      "kind": "intent",
      "text": "A round records which children answer yes in the actual world (said-yes(c, r)), and rules out every world where some child would answer differently than in the actual world (all answers are heard).",
      "stmts": [
        4
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "A-MC5",
      "kind": "intent",
      "text": "The goal is that every child has answered yes in some round; the rounds of first yes are read from said-yes. Four rounds are provided.",
      "stmts": [
        6
      ]
    }
  ],
